WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.344
Part eight.

00:00:01.344 --> 00:00:03.734
Highlights and notes on any page.

00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:10.933
Pocket QA also lets you mark up web pages, say, while reading your team's testing guide on the blog.

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:14.442
Select some text, and a colour picker pops up next to it.

00:00:14.442 --> 00:00:15.634
Choose yellow.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:19.971
Mark the important part in green, and add a note for the team.

00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:35.148
Hover a highlight to read its note.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:42.407
The Highlight tab lists them all, counted per page, with search and colour filters.

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:50.565
Reload the page and they're all still there, even on content that loads late.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:57.151
URL patterns let pages with the same layout share one set, and Export saves everything as JSON.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.774
From here on, we move to the data tools, starting with SQL.
